<title>FRANCE: Salins shares surge 37 pct after bid.</title>
<headline>Salins shares surge 37 pct after bid.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-01-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in salt company Cie des Salins du Midi, which resumed trading on Friday for the first time since December 23, surged 37 percent to 607 francs, close to the 614 franc per share offer proposed on Tuesday by Morton International.</p>
<p>Morton said it would buy the 50.8 percent controlling stake in Cie des Salins from a Compagnie de Suez subsidiary and offer the same price to minority shareholders. The bid values Cie des Salins at 1.5 billion francs.</p>
<p>The share was the top gainer on the Paris bourse, rising 167 francs to 607 at 1020 GMT.</p>
</text>
